flowchart LR
  subgraph env["One uv-managed venv — one Python, ordinary Python package deps only"]
    app["User Python app\n(app.py setup(rt) — normal codebase;\nhosts no processor)"]
    procs["User processor classes\n(importable modules — imported by the app\nto register, by helpers to run;\nnever hosted in the app;\nthe class's import path is its identity)"]
    pkgs["Processor packages\n(ordinary PyPI packages; native internals\nexpose handles, never streamlib internals;\nfirst-party optional integrations live in packages/,\nlocal-linked in-repo, published via the wheel's index)"]
    wheel["streamlib wheel\n(Python API + CLI + engine, PyO3 —\nrepo releases now, PyPI after rename)"]
    helper["Helper processes — every Python processor\n(engine exec of sys.executable; own\ninterpreter, own GIL; imports the wheel;\nthe only placement)"]
  end

  rustapp["Rust app\n(plain cargo project)"]
  crate["streamlib crate\n(embeddable Rust library)"]
  engine["Engine runtime\n(runtime/streamlib-engine)"]
  media["Built-in media blocks\n(camera / display / MicrophoneSource / SpeakerSink — native,\nin the wheel, handle-shaped primitives;\naudio backend dlopen'd: PipeWire → ALSA → null,\nchosen by opening not by loading; vendored SPA headers\ncompile to a shim that calls only pointers, so no audio\nlibrary enters DT_NEEDED;\ndevice-paced, conditioning on the built-ins;\ncodec blocks: H264/H265 encode+decode shipped on Vulkan Video sessions,\none encode body and one decode body specialised by codec identity,\ncolour conversion on the engine's existing rgb_to_nv12 — no new RHI primitive;\nall four reach Python as marker classes like every other built-in, and the\nencoded frame has a Python cast (EncodedVideoFrame) holding no surface;\nOpus encode+decode shipped over statically linked libopus, and a pure-Rust\nfragmented Mp4Sink muxing both — one track per inbound link, named by its channel;\nJpegDecoder still to come — an encoded frame is an\nordinary bag, bitstream inline as bin beside the ordering pair and sync-point flag;\nan encoded audio packet is that convention applied to audio, cast by EncodedAudioPacket;\na decoder publishes the SPS display window, never the padded coded picture)"]
  rhi["RHI\n(vulkan/rhi + streamlib-consumer-rhi)"]
  interop["Interop adapters\n(Vulkan↔CUDA, Vulkan↔GL — app-process Rust)"]
  ctl["Control plane\n(api-server: HTTP / WS / MCP — engine-side)"]
  cli["CLI (in the wheel)\nnew / dev / run · nodes / graph / tap / logs / exchange"]
  wire["Wire\n(self-describing bags between nodes —\nthe only cross-language boundary)"]

  registry["Node registry\n(per-user on-disk, one JSON per live node)"]

  app -->|imports classes for rt.add| procs
  app -->|imports classes for rt.add| pkgs
  procs --> helper
  pkgs --> helper
  helper -->|"raw memory fd, Full-gated — names the allocation, never the
frame; the importer adopts it and consumes it as an image"| pkgs
  app --> wheel
  wheel --> engine
  engine -->|"bags carry per-frame surface ids (slot#generation);
claim at typed cast, lease until drop;
a stale id errors, never another frame;
the cast object is the tensor-protocol producer —
bare DLPack reads, scoped writes publishing at the block edge;
the CPU door maps pixels in the child — the surface's own coherent
mapping, or its host-visible staging over a texture backing;
pixel bytes never ride the escalate socket;
audio rides the bag itself — AudioBlock samples inline, no surface ids;
a windowed input port is resampled, channel-converted and framed at this read
seam, and reports ready only when a full window can be emitted — a gap flushes
the accumulator and the resampler's filter rather than interpolating across it;
its channel count is the contract's one optional value: absent means the source's own
count, carried on every emitted window, and a declared count is what the stage converts to;
every input port declares one read policy — newest or ordered — and no other delivery setting:
both drop under pressure, and no link ever blocks a producer;
a drop is counted at the port that lost it, but only an app-process destination's
count reaches graph — a helper's counts stay in its own child process (OPEN);
a read can name the inbound link a bag arrived on, and a port can list the links wired
into it — which is how a many-track sink learns what it owes, counting unchanged;
every stamp reads the one machine-monotonic clock"| helper
  helper -->|"kernels constructed in setup(), dispatched by name and
synchronously — one submission per batch; an output is named by surface id,
and a DLPack scope over it is the optional third-party read / write-back;
a processor-owned window is requested in setup() and fed by named frames —
the engine runs its native present loop, latest-wins"| engine
  ctl --> registry
  rustapp --> crate
  crate --> engine
  media -->|"one audio device seam — AudioDeviceBackend opening capture /
playback streams, an engine primitive beside the audio clock;
the built-ins, the null backend and every test open through it,
and a stream that dies reports to its owner;
the device stamps the block and the engine never re-stamps it;
SpeakerSink declares audio_window = match_device and settles it at setup()
from the format the device opened, so the stage converts and the sink plays"| engine
  engine --> rhi
  engine --> interop
  ctl -->|"one RuntimeOperations handle, never engine internals;
exchange claims a published surface id, converts and copies it in the RHI,
releases, then encodes — exact PNG over REST, a capped image block over MCP;
a retired id is refused, never answered with the slot's newer pixels;
the codec proof rig scores off this door — tap the decoded channel, exchange each
sampled id for exact pixels — never off a display writing frames to disk"| engine
  cli --> ctl
  engine --> wire
